 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Probed with scratch ticket RD-1016 \"{{v2}}\" (customer Probe). Mark Ready with no parts was REFUSED with error text \"Ticket is not ready\" and unmet list: [\"A ticket needs at least one part before it can be marked Ready\"]; after adding one part (name \"Probe part\", cost 0, markup 0, no supplier) it was REFUSED again with \"Ticket is not ready\" + [\"Part \\\"Probe part\\\" has no supplier\"]; setting that part's Supplier to \"Probe supplier\" was the change that made Mark Ready succeed (status → Ready, no error shown, buttons became Mark Draft/Mark Closed). So the app requires (1) ≥1 part and (2) a supplier on every part — cost 0 / markup 0 did not matter. Note the part form's own hint calls Supplier \"Optional. Leave blank if the part has not been sourced yet\", which contradicts the precondition. The app exposes no ticket-delete control (only Archive/Unarchive; the sole DELETE in app.js is for parts), so I archived the scratch ticket: it is now absent from the default Tickets list and appears as \"RD-1016 | {{v2}} Archived | Probe | Ready | 1 | 2026-09-17\" only with \"Show archived\" ticked.",
